# Power moves to the other guide in lambda / (2 (n_even - n_odd)) = 20.37 um, from the supermodes of the transverse grid.
# Reference: full transfer at that length, half at half of it. Monitors use the modes of the separate guides, which overlap slightly at small gaps.
title Directional coupler, two 0.5 um guides 200 nm apart
window width=14 length=42.75
guide straight x=-0.35 width=0.5 from=0 to=42.75
guide straight x=0.35 width=0.5 from=0 to=42.75
launch mode x=-0.35 width=0.5
monitor half_cross z=10.25 x=0.35 width=0.5
monitor cross_full z=20.25 x=0.35 width=0.5
monitor bar_full z=20.25 x=-0.35 width=0.5
monitor bar_end z=42.75 x=-0.35 width=0.5
monitor cross_end z=42.75 x=0.35 width=0.5
expect power half_cross 0.505797145 2e-7
expect power cross_full 0.997809020 2e-7
expect power bar_full 0.002812010 2e-7
expect power bar_end 0.975487005 2e-7
expect power cross_end 0.026250017 2e-7
expect neff 2.648884804 2e-8
expect power_above cross_full 0.995
expect power_below bar_full 0.005
expect power half_cross 0.5 0.02
expect sum bar_end cross_end 1.0 0.002
